              Name: (string) "",
              Type: (string) (len=9) "paragraph",
              Value: (string) (len=601) "When filming the scene in The Empire Strikes Back in which Vader confesses he is Luke's father, Prowse was given modified dialogue to read that did not exist in the script. He was known for repeatedly leaking information to the public, and the filmmakers wanted to keep Vader's revelation a secret until the film was released. Prowse was asked to read the line \"Obi-Wan killed your father\" instead of \"No, I am your father.\" Only the director, the producers, and Mark Hamill knew the actual line, which was dubbed in later by Jones. Prowse did not know the real line until he viewed the finished film.",
